how to handle odata batch processing in sap cpi?
A.Batch processing in the OData adapter of SAP Cloud Platform Integration
 (SAP CPI) allows multiple operations to be grouped into a single request,
  improving performance and reducing network overhead.

  Handling Batch Processing in OData CPI Adapter

  1. Batch Processing in OData V2
  - Supported Operations: POST, PUT, MERGE, DELETE
  - ChangeSets: Groups multiple operations that must be processed together.
  - Configuration:
  - Enable Batch Processing ($batch) in the adapter.
  - Define ChangeSets for transactional consistency.
  - Structure the payload using <batchParts> and <batchChangeSet> tags.



  2. Batch Processing in OData V4
  - Supported Operations: GET, POST, PUT, DELETE
  - BatchSet & ChangeSet:
  - BatchSet: Used for data retrieval requests.
  - ChangeSet: Used for data modification requests.
  - Configuration:
  - Select Batch Processing ($batch) in the adapter.
  - Define ChangeSets for transactional updates.
  - Use an EDMX file to structure the payload.

  3. Benefits of Batch Processing
  ✔ Reduces API calls by grouping multiple operations.
  ✔ Improves performance by minimizing network latency.
  ✔ Ensures consistency with ChangeSets (all operations succeed or fail together).
